#HSSS 1.0
TITLE: Ubuntu White Edition / systemd Specification
PACKAGE: systemd
LANGUAGE: C
STATUS: W2
ROLE: Boot, service lifecycle, supervision, logging, session, resource management

## PROGRAM
systemd manages boot targets, service activation, process supervision, logging integration, sessions, and selected resource controls.

## STRUCTURE
SOURCE: upstream systemd / Ubuntu package
BOUNDARY: boot -> targets -> units -> processes -> IPC/logging/resource policy
WHITE_EDITION: configuration, policy, tests, documentation; source changes only when justified
GUI: JavaFX administration may use supported service interfaces and authorization boundaries

## SPEC
- predictable dependency ordering
- explicit privilege boundaries
- observable failure and recovery
- controlled resource policies
- deterministic service configuration

## QUALITY
TEST: boot target, lifecycle, dependency failure, privilege, journal, resource, recovery, upgrade
ECONOMY: boot time, resident memory, activation cost, journal growth, CPU

## SOURCE POLICY
Systemd is primarily C. Native changes require a concrete reliability/security requirement and focused regression evidence.
